WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.960
Who you serve, how clients arrive, and getting outreach-ready.

2
00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:08.290
This is the video for Module 1 of Client Acquisition Basics.

3
00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:15.820
Many skilled women are very good at their work, but get clients only by chance, then nothing for weeks.

4
00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:23.570
Client acquisition is a separate skill from your service. And like any skill, it can be learned and practised.

5
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:31.990
It means finding people who need your service, starting conversations with them, and turning the right ones into paying clients.

6
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:42.910
Inbound means clients come to you. Outbound means you go to them. This course focuses on outbound and referrals, because those are the parts you control.

7
00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:53.410
Every client you have ever had passed through five stages. First, a prospect. That is a specific business or person who could need your service.

8
00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:01.410
Second, a conversation. They have replied to you, and a reply of any kind, even 'not now', moves them here.

9
00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:09.160
Third, qualified. You have checked they have a real need, can pay, can decide, and want it soon enough to matter.

10
00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:14.960
Fourth, a proposal. You have sent a clear offer with scope, price and timing.

11
00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:21.240
Fifth, a client. They have agreed in writing and paid a deposit or the full fee.

12
00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:28.610
Each stage has fewer people than the one before, so always start with more prospects than the clients you want.

13
00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:36.180
For example, Ngozi runs a small bookkeeping service in Enugu. She wants 2 new monthly clients.

14
00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:43.100
She guesses that half of her calls become clients. So for 2 clients, she needs 4 calls.

15
00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:51.120
She guesses 1 in every 3 people who reply will agree to a call. So 4 calls need 12 replies.

16
00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:59.640
And she guesses 3 people reply for every 10 personal messages. So 12 replies need 40 messages.

17
00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:06.990
40 messages a month is about 2 every working day. A small daily habit, not a vague hope.

18
00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:11.710
These are cautious guesses. Replace them with your own numbers after a month.

19
00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:22.270
'I do social media for anybody' sounds flexible, but you cannot search for anybody. So you write an ideal client profile, with four parts.

20
00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:27.270
Industry. For example, private nursery and primary schools.

21
00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:35.220
Size, and who decides. For example, 100 to 400 pupils, where the proprietor decides.

22
00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:41.400
Location. Where you can serve well, such as Kaduna North and Kaduna South.

23
00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:53.020
And the trigger, the part most people forget. It is a visible event that creates a need, like admissions season for a school. It tells you who to contact and why now.

24
00:02:53.370 --> 00:03:00.260
If you can find at least 30 real businesses in under 20 minutes on Google Maps, your profile is reachable.

25
00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:13.620
For example, Halima manages social media. Her old line said she does social media, graphics and content for businesses at affordable prices. Every competitor says the same.

26
00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:25.160
Her new line says she helps Kaduna nursery and primary schools get more parent enquiries before each admissions season, with weekly posts and forwardable flyers.

27
00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:28.640
Name the client and the result, in under 30 words.

28
00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:40.560
When you message a prospect, she will check you in seconds. So first, set up a clear profile. Use the free WhatsApp Business app, with your business name and your offer sentence.

29
00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:46.120
Second, simple honest proof. 2 to 4 real examples are enough.

30
00:03:47.370 --> 00:04:00.450
Third, decide your price range before you talk. For example, Chioma, a designer, worked out that a one-page menu is usually around 40,000 naira, approximately, from her time and costs.

31
00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:06.430
Some strangers are not genuine. Before you start work, tick every box.

32
00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:11.840
Check the business is real, talk to a real person, and agree the scope in writing.

33
00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:22.260
Confirm the deposit in your bank app, because screenshots can be faked. Never pay a registration or vendor fee to get a contract. Genuine clients pay you.

34
00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:27.470
And never share your BVN, card PIN, OTP codes or passwords.

35
00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:38.320
So remember. Client acquisition is a skill you can learn. Work backwards from your target to a daily number, and aim at one clear profile with a trigger.

36
00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:44.220
And do not work free to prove yourself. Use a small, clearly priced starter offer instead.

37
00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:50.800
Now it is your turn. Find your stuck stage, write your offer, and get your profile ready.

38
00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.090
Continue with the lessons below.
